   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm certain actions taken by the village of Hammond, in the county of St. Lawrence, with respect to a certain serial bond note",
    "basePrintNo": "S5951",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5951-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Villages",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5951\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm certain actions taken\nby the village of Hammond, in the county of St. Lawrence, with respect\nto a certain serial bond note\n\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\nThe legislation is to provide legislative relief by validating and\nratifying the actions of the Village of Hammond, NY with respect to\nthe subject of certain inadvertent minor late payments made involving\ncurrent borrowing. It should be noted that no payments have been\nmissed and the village of Hammond is not in default. The legislation\nis designed to hold the village harmless from those minor late\npayments.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis legislation provides an explanation the issue in which the\nVillage of Hammond, NY had issued serial bonds for $800,000 to finance\nthe cost of a capital improvement project for wastewater collection\nand that several principal payments were not made in a timely fashion\nand that the village now wishes to obtain permanent financing from the\nEnvironmental Facilities Corporation to refund the subject note.\n\nThe legislation validates and ratifies the USDA note.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Village of Hammond is seeking to obtain permanent financing\nthrough the Environmental Facilities Corporation, and in order to do\nso, must validate and ratify the USDA note. The Village made several\nlate payments on the existing note and these actions rendered the\nVillage unable to obtain permanent financing. This legislation\nvalidates and ratifies the note so that the village can be eligible to\nobtain permanent financing.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nUnknown at this time.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
